---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const personSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Santiago González',
  url: 'https://brandsbuilders.ca/about',
  jobTitle: 'Founder',
  worksFor: { '@id': 'https://brandsbuilders.ca/#business' },
  sameAs: ['https://brandsbuilders.ca'],
};

const seo = {
  title: 'About — BrandsBuilders | Santiago González',
  description: 'BrandsBuilders helps HVAC, Roofing, and Restoration businesses build referral networks that produce ~60 jobs/year from 4–5 strategic partners.',
  canonical: 'https://brandsbuilders.ca/about',
  schema: personSchema,
};
---

<Layout seo={seo}>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-white pt-16 pb-14 border-b border-gray-200">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-orange-50 border border-orange-200 text-orange-700 text-xs font-semibold mb-6">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-orange-500 shrink-0"></span>
        BrandsBuilders
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-5 leading-tight">
        Built by Santiago González
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
        I build referral networks for HVAC, Roofing, and Restoration businesses — and custom websites for local trades that want to stop renting their visibility from Google Ads.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Story -->
  <section class="bg-white py-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none space-y-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-[17px]">

        <p>
          I noticed something working with trades businesses: the ones with the best growth often had nothing to do with ads. They had a plumber who sent them every water damage job. An adjuster who referred roof claims. A property manager with a 50-unit portfolio who used them exclusively for HVAC.
        </p>

        <p>
          Those relationships were built by accident — usually a casual conversation at a job site or a chance meeting. The businesses that had them were thriving. The ones without them were spending heavily on ads chasing leads that price-shopped three other companies before calling.
        </p>

        <p>
          The difference wasn't the quality of the work. It was who sent the job and why.
        </p>

        <p>
          A referral from a trusted source arrives pre-sold. The homeowner isn't shopping — they're calling because someone they trust said "use these guys." Close rate doubles. CAC drops to near zero. And unlike ad spend, a good referral network compounds: partners who trust you send more over time, not less.
        </p>

        <p>
          So I started building these networks deliberately — mapping the ecosystem around a trades business, identifying the 4–5 highest-leverage partner types, recruiting the actual businesses, and setting up the relationship so it stays active without a retainer.
        </p>

        <p>
          That's what BrandsBuilders does.
        </p>

        <p>
          We also build websites — custom-coded, fast, conversion-focused — for trades businesses that want a real web presence without the WordPress headache or ongoing maintenance fees. It's a separate offer, and it's one-time.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Values / How I work -->
  <section class="bg-gray-50 py-16 border-y border-gray-200">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">How I work</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
        {[
          { title: 'Honest about fit', body: 'If the referral network model doesn\'t fit your niche or market, I\'ll tell you on the call — not after you\'ve paid.' },
          { title: 'You own everything', body: 'The network, the relationships, the website code. No lock-in, no retainer dependency, no data held hostage.' },
          { title: 'One point of contact', body: 'You deal with me directly — not an account manager or an outsourced team. Response within 24 hours.' },
          { title: 'No upsells', body: 'The referral network is a one-time engagement. If you want more after that, we can discuss it. But I\'m not going to manufacture dependency.' },
        ].map(item => (
          <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="bg-gray-900 text-white py-16 text-center">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-3">Want to see if your niche fits?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8 text-lg">Book a 15-min call. I'll tell you exactly which partner types are in your market and what the network looks like before you decide anything.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a href="/apply" class="inline-flex px-9 py-4 rounded-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 bg-white hover:bg-gray-100 transition text-lg">
          See which partners fit you →
        </a>
        <a href="https://cal.com/brandsbuilders/30-min" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex px-9 py-4 rounded-lg font-semibold text-white border border-gray-700 hover:border-gray-500 transition text-lg">
          Book a 15-min call
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
